From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:40:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: discard completed frame flush state before video cleanup

Video encoder disable leaves the last completed frame's software flush mask
intact. Pipeline cleanup unstages the SSPPs, but includes those old SSPP
bits in its teardown flush. On MSM8953 those bits can remain pending while
their pipes are inactive and survive the following enable.

A failure trace shows the final frame's 0x22858 flush completing,
then teardown issuing 0x40022858 with no pipes staged. The next DMA-only
enable completes its 0x40022840 mask and receives four vblanks, but the
unrelated RGB 0x18 bits still block the whole-register completion waiter.

Start the cleanup mask from scratch after the timing engine is stopped,
as the writeback disable path already does. Cleanup builds its own mixer,
interface and auxiliary-block flush mask. Leave the hardware completion
predicate, genuine timeout handling and normal plane selection unchanged.

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/msm8953-mainline/linux
Base-commit: 755ffc44d5d8442adeec8bbaa02108478089c4d7
Apply in filename order within this project.


---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
index ba810f26ea3099106aac1783f7f6bf5e014e41a0..1df8e5d82795a97f99718db75197bc8421873fe4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -645,6 +645,9 @@ static void dpu_encoder_phys_vid_disable(struct dpu_encoder_phys *phys_enc)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Build the teardown flush without the last completed frame's SSPPs. */
+	phys_enc->hw_ctl->ops.clear_pending_flush(phys_enc->hw_ctl);
+
 	dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup(phys_enc);
 	phys_enc->enable_state = DPU_ENC_DISABLED;
 }
